# Stack & Conventions — fohlioo-app

## Stack

- **Next.js 14, App Router** — no Pages Router. Server Components by
  default; add `"use client"` only where interactivity requires it.
- **TypeScript, strict mode.** No `any` without a comment explaining why.
- **Tailwind CSS** for all styling. No CSS modules, no styled-components.
- **Supabase Auth** for identity (email/password + Google OAuth). Supabase
  Postgres is shared with fohlioo-api — this app reads/writes via the
  Supabase client using the user's own session (RLS-scoped), never the
  service role key. The service role key belongs only in fohlioo-api.
- **Zod** for all form validation and API route input validation.

## Folder structure

```
app/
├── (marketing)/           # public landing page, pricing, about — no auth required
│   └── page.tsx
├── auth/
│   ├── login/page.tsx
│   ├── signup/page.tsx
│   └── extension/page.tsx # extension handoff flow — see 20-auth-architecture.mdc
├── dashboard/
│   ├── shopper/           # shopper-facing dashboard, requires shopper session
│   └── brand/             # brand-facing dashboard, requires brand session
├── api/
│   └── auth/
│       └── extension-code/route.ts  # generates one-time handoff code
lib/
├── supabase/
│   ├── client.ts          # browser client
│   └── server.ts          # server component / route handler client
├── auth/
│   └── session.ts         # session helpers, role checks (shopper vs brand)
components/
├── ui/                    # shared primitives
├── marketing/
└── dashboard/
```

## Conventions

- **Route protection**: use middleware (`middleware.ts`) to redirect
  unauthenticated users away from `/dashboard/*`, and to redirect shoppers
  away from `/dashboard/brand/*` and vice versa. Don't scatter auth checks
  ad hoc inside individual pages.
- **Server Actions over API routes** for form submissions where possible
  (signup, login, profile updates). Reserve `app/api/*` route handlers for
  things external clients call — specifically the extension handoff code
  endpoint, and anything the Chrome extension itself needs to hit.
- **Never trust client-submitted `user_id` or `shopper_id`.** Always derive
  identity from the verified Supabase session server-side.
- **Naming**: `snake_case` for database columns (matches fohlioo-api's
  Supabase schema), `camelCase` for TypeScript variables/functions. Map at
  the query boundary, don't leak snake_case into component props.
- **No new database tables or columns without checking fohlioo-api's
  `supabase/schema.sql` first** — the schema is shared infrastructure, not
  owned by this repo alone. If a feature needs a schema change, flag it
  explicitly rather than silently adding a migration here.
